                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "The CI job fetches and runs staticcheck at a version tag through the Go module proxy. The Go checksum database verifies it, and the job has default checkout-only permissions. No exploit is reachable from this change, so this is a hardening note only.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  ".github/workflows/ci.yml:524-526"
                ],
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "I reviewed all 22 manifest paths. The change adds a standard-library-only Go module, so it adds no third-party dependency and no lockfile.",
              "Log files and the meta file are opened read-only. The record struct decodes only usage, id, model and timestamp fields. Output holds aggregates, and the tests assert that the sentinel content never reaches stdout.",
              "The log roots and price file path come from local CLI flags. There is no network input, no shell execution and no privilege boundary. I found no injection, traversal or secret exposure that is reachable.",
              "Price parsing rejects duplicate keys, unknown fields, trailing data, and NaN, Infinity or negative rates. This limits unsafe input handling.",
              "The two review-receipt JSON files are metadata only. They contain no secrets."
            ]
          }
