            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "I reviewed all 22 manifest paths. The change adds a new read-only Go module and one CI job, and it alters no existing runtime behavior.",
              "Failure handling degrades gracefully in telemetry/readers.go. Walk errors and unopenable files increment UnreadableFiles and the walk continues. A file that fails mid-read is dropped whole, and its Pi IDs are not recorded as seen. ReadBytes means oversized lines do not abort the read. Malformed lines are counted as Skipped. A missing or invalid meta file gives an empty agentType.",
              "telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main.go skips a missing default root with a note. An explicit missing root exits 1, and so does having no readable source. A bad price file exits 1 before any log is read. The readable check uses stats.Read, which counts only files read to the end, so a root where every file is unreadable exits 1.",
              "Memory is O(calls) for the retained context and cost slices and the per-file row map. The ledger records about 87k calls and about 9 s on the real corpus. I found no measured load or latency failure.",
              "Retry safety holds. Logs are opened read-only, and the same input gives byte-identical output through sorted emission and canonical-order cost sums.",
              "I found no concrete production failure that this change caused and that realistic input can reach."
            ]
          }
        }
