            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 22 manifest paths. The change is a new standalone module plus one new CI job, so it has no baseline regression surface.",
              "telemetry/readers_test.go covers the failure paths with observable Stats and Call assertions. It covers malformed lines, 2 MB lines, a missing root, a broken symlink, an unreadable directory, a mid-read I/O error that drops the file, bad or missing meta files, and Pi fallback-ID scoping per file.",
              "Output is deterministic. Readers sort emission by timestamp then ID, group keys are sorted, and costs are summed in sorted order. telemetry/aggregate_test.go checks shuffled insertion order for both recorded and estimated costs.",
              "telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main_test.go asserts exit codes 0, 1 and 2, skipping of a missing default root, an error for an explicit missing root, 'no readable source', price-file errors, byte-equal golden output and a no-modification check on the fixtures.",
              "telemetry/prices_test.go rejects duplicate keys, unknown fields, trailing data, NaN, Infinity, overflow, negative rates and null or missing rates. Matching is by exact model ID, and a recorded cost is never re-estimated.",
              "The fixture totals and the golden report in telemetry/testdata/golden/report.txt agree with the fixture inputs. For example, the Claude main call is deduped to output 100 and the synthetic and malformed lines are skipped.",
              "Minor edge case I did not report: a log file placed directly at the root yields its file name as the project. This is low impact and not exercised by realistic corpus layouts."
            ]
          }
        }
